From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:22:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Answer isChunkLoaded from the full chunk map

isChunkLoaded looked up the chunk holder and then its FULL chunk, several
dependent loads per call. Plugins sweeping loaded chunks call it for
every chunk. The full chunk map is updated in the same step as the
holder's FULL status (onChunkPreBorder right after the status becomes
FULL, onChunkPostNotBorder right before it drops), with no plugin code
in between, so its lookup gives the same answer.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerChunkCache.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerChunkCache.java
index cc305c6644af627d25d839e00cd7047cb21bb72d..20641a630fa71ab7b2f94f9b2d68ad2cbb296a58 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerChunkCache.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerChunkCache.java
@@ -251,11 +251,8 @@ public class ServerChunkCache extends ChunkSource implements ca.spottedleaf.moon
 
     // CraftBukkit start - properly implement isChunkLoaded
     public boolean isChunkLoaded(int chunkX, int chunkZ) {
-        ChunkHolder chunk = this.chunkMap.getUpdatingChunkIfPresent(ChunkPos.pack(chunkX, chunkZ));
-        if (chunk == null) {
-            return false;
-        }
-        return chunk.getFullChunkNow() != null;
+        // Pyzh - The full chunk map changes together with the holder's FULL status, with no plugin code in between
+        return this.getChunkAtIfLoadedImmediately(chunkX, chunkZ) != null;
     }
     // CraftBukkit end
     // Paper start
